# Line-ending policy.
#
# `*.patch eol=lf` is load-bearing: cmake/Dependencies.cmake feeds these files
# to `git apply` against ggml sources extracted from an upstream tarball
# (LF-only).  A checkout with core.autocrlf=true (the default on Windows and
# on GitHub windows runners) converts a text file's working-tree copy to
# CRLF, and `git apply` then rejects the patch ("patch does not apply") even
# though the committed blob is correct.  Forcing LF at checkout keeps the
# patch byte-identical to what was committed, on every platform.
*.patch text eol=lf

# Conventional hygiene for the few file types where endings actually matter.
*.sh   text eol=lf
*.bat  text eol=crlf
*.png  binary
*.ico  binary
*.icns binary
